      "file": "libvips/foreign/matrixload.c",
      "function": "vips_foreign_load_matrix_load",
      "line": 232,
      "code": "line = vips_sbuf_get_line_copy( matrix->sbuf );",
      "note": "First project-side statement on the crashing row that materializes attacker-controlled row bytes into vulnerability-relevant heap state. After the valid matrix header has admitted this loader, `vips_sbuf_get_line_copy()` copies the current untrusted data row into heap buffer `line`.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "libvips/foreign/matrixload.c",
      "function": "vips_foreign_load_matrix_load",
      "line": null,
      "code": "g_free( line );",
      "note": "The parser frees the row buffer before reporting the conversion error. Because `p` still aliases the current token inside `line`, the subsequent `vips_error(..., p)` call uses a dangling pointer. The staged fix removes this use-after-free by moving `g_free(line)` after `vips_error(...)`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
